# Cloudflare Pages redirect rules. One per line: from, to, status.
#
# The site lives under /en-us/ because the URL was asked for in that shape.
# Nothing is translated yet, so the locale is a promise rather than a fact —
# dropping it later means deleting these four lines and moving the directory
# back up.
#
# The short paths are here because they are what people type and what the app
# used to point at. They cost nothing and they stop a mistyped link being a
# 404 in somebody's hand.
#
# **www is not handled here.** A `_redirects` rule matches a path, not a host,
# so www -> apex has to be a Redirect Rule in the Cloudflare dashboard. Adding
# a rule here that looks like it covers www would be worse than having none.

/            /en-us/            301
/privacy     /en-us/privacy/    301
/terms       /en-us/terms/      301
/cookies     /en-us/cookies/    301
/support     /en-us/support/    301
